  "title": "The Laundry Label Mystery",
  "family": "fiction",
  "category": "everyday microdramas",
  "premise": "A figure wants to pair socks from a basket, but every sock carries a confusing abstract tag. Instead of deciphering the tags, they lay the socks heel-to-heel and compare shape and length, making pairs; the final unmatched sock becomes a puppet who proudly introduces the basket.",
  "hook": "Every sock has a label. None of them help.",
  "visible_action": "Tags flap; socks fan across the floor; heels align; pairs fold together; lone sock rises as a speaking puppet.",
  "intended_takeaway_or_theme": "Use the features that actually answer the immediate question.",
  "gate": "This is a matching gag, not care-label or textile-cleaning advice.",
